  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n\nOur approach combines deterministic gradient methods with randomized exploration to overcome the challenges of the discontinuous correlation objective. The key innovation is a \"wiggle\" perturbation technique that maintains integral constraints while allowing escape from local minima. We use automatic differentiation to compute gradients and apply them in a structured sequence, followed by purpose-built repair procedures. The method balances global exploration through Gaussian noise with local refinement through alternating gradient descent and coordinate optimization.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n\nVariables:\n- h[i] \u2208 [0,1] for i \u2208 0..n_points-1\n- Integral constraint: (1/dx)\u2211h[i] = 1\n\nObjective:\nC5 = (dx) * max_k [\u2211h[i] * (1-h[i+k % n_points])]\n\nConstraints:\n- Box constraints: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n- Integral constraint: (1/dx)\u2211h[i] = 1\n\nRepair mechanism:\n- Initialized from either parent or uniform noise\n- Projection to grid: clip to [0,1] then redistribute discrepancy\n\nDifferentiation:\n- Forward-mode AD to compute gradient of np.correlate\n- For F (the full correlation array), the gradient of C5 is the gradient of max(F)*dx\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n\n<implementation>\n// n_points is given by initial_h_values.shape[0]\ndef run(seed=42, budget_s=1300, **kwargs):\n    n_points = len(initial_h_values)\n    dx = 2.0 / n_points\n    target_sum = n_points / 2.0  // For integral = 1 under dx\n    \n    # Initial seed: clone parent or use uniform perturbation\n    h = initial_h_values.astype(float) + 0.01 * np.random.randn(n_points)\n    h = project_feasible(h, target_sum)\n    \n    best_score = float('inf')\n    history = [compute_c5(h)]\n    \n    # Time tracking\n    start_time = time.time()\n    time_remaining = budget_s\n    \n    # Optimization parameters\n    eta_heuristic = [0.03, 0.1, 0.3, 1.0]  # Step sizes\n    nld_delta_values = [d/float(t) for d,t in zip([2,-2,5,-5,10,-10], range(1,7))]\n    iteration = 0\n    max_iter = int(300 * (n_points/400)**1.5)  // Sample-based iteration limit\n    \n    for _ in range(max_iter):\n        if time_remaining <= 10: break\n        \n        iteration += 1\n        time_per_iter = time_remaining / max_iter\n        eta = eta_heuristic[(iteration % 4)]\n        ndx = iteration0_400 = n_points/400\n        \n        # Repair and Gradient descent phase\n        grad_mag_initial = compute_descent_direction(h, dx)\n        decent_phase(\n            h, dx, target_sum, initial=h.copy(), \n            eta=eta, max_iter=10, time_budget=time_per_iter*0.05)\n        \n        # Coordinate-descent refinement\n        best_candidate, best_score_candidate = coordinate_descent_phase(\n            h, target_sum, time_limit=time_per_iter*0.1)\n        score_candidate = compute_c5(best_candidate)\n        \n        # Track statistics\n        current_score = compute_c5(h)\n        history.append(min(score_candidate, current_score))\n        \n        # Wiggle phase: probabilistic escape from local optima\n        if iteration % 60 == 0 or np.random.rand() < 0.05 or grad_mag_initial < 1e-4:\n            h = wiggled_adaptive_attack(\n                h, dx, target_sum, eta=eta, nld_delta_values=nld_delta_values,\n                max_iter=15, time_budget=time_per_iter*0.8)\n            time_remaining -= time_per_iter\n        \n        # Repair non-feasible states\n        h = project_feasible(h, target_sum)\n    \n    return h, min(history), n_points\n\n# Requires helper functions: decent_phase(), wiggled_adaptive_attack(), coordinate_descent_phase(), project_feasible(), compute_c5()\n</implementation>\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n\nHyperparameter tuning:\n- eta_heuristic adpatation by iteration mod 4\n- delta_values for coordinate descent tailored by ndx (rough estimate ratio)\n- Time allocation between descent and coordinate descent phases\n- Gradient descent: uses analytic projection to maintain constraint\n- Wiggle phase: applies context-aware perturbations proportional to gradient magnitude\n\nPeriodic repair invoked when:\n- Gradient magnitude falls below 1e-4\n- Mothr 60 iterations of optimization\n- 5% random exit probability to escape solutions\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n\nComplexity:\n- Objective evaluations: O(n_points^2) primarily from np.correlate\n- Gradient computation: O(n_points^2) via AD\n- Coordinate descent: O(iterations * n_points)\n- Wiggle: O(iterations * n_points)\n\nEstimates:\nFrom the provided code base and numpy implementation:\n  correlation: uses FFT => O(n_points log n_points)\n  projec -tion: O(n_points)\n\nTime limits:\n- Use time_remaining as proxy for iteration count\n- For budget of 1300s with n_points=400:\n    - ~300-400 iterations achievable\n    - Subsidiary coordination of gradients is manageable\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n\nOutput contracts:\n- h = array-like: after projection\n- score = float: C5 value from compute_c5(h)\n- n_points = int\n\nChecks:\n- Integral constraint: np(sum(h)) \u2248 n/2 within 1e-5 tolerance\n- Bounds: all(h[i]) \u2208 [0,1] for all i\n- Feasibility: h from project_feasible ensures integral and bounds\n- Objectives: compute_c5(h) returns designed finite value\n\nRepair functionality:\n- project_feasible(h, target_sum) handles:\n    - Box clipping followed by redistribution\n    - Avoids overflow by using iterative clip-and-distribute\n    - Correctly maintains integral under adjustments\n\nNote: this code will need careful implementation to ensure all boundary conditions are met. The gradient descent phase uses a descent direction computed using AD whereas the coordinate_descent_phase uses a specialized refinement. Each step maintains the integral constraint through projection, ensuring valid solutions throughout the search.",
